=== ) goes to the start of the next sentence
ref:    motion.txt *)*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s forward.  |exclusive| motion."
given:  |Hello there. How are you?
keys:   )
expect: Hello there. |How are you?

=== 2) with a count
ref:    motion.txt *)*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s forward."
given:  |One. Two! Three? Four.
keys:   2)
expect: One. Two! |Three? Four.

=== ) skips the run of spaces after the sentence end
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  "A sentence is defined as ending at a '.', '!' or '?' followed by either the end of a line, or by a space or tab."
given:  |One.   Two.
keys:   )
expect: One.   |Two.

=== a period not followed by white space does not end a sentence
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  "A sentence is defined as ending at a '.', '!' or '?' followed by either the end of a line, or by a space or tab."
given:  |a.b c. d
keys:   )
expect: a.b c. |d

=== closing quotes and brackets may follow the sentence end
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  "Any number of closing ')', ']', '\"' and ''' characters may appear after the '.', '!' or '?' before the spaces, tabs or end of line."
given:  |He said "Hi.") Then
keys:   )
expect: He said "Hi.") |Then

=== a sentence ending at the end of a line continues on the next
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  "followed by either the end of a line"
given:
  |One.
  Two.
keys:   )
expect:
  One.
  |Two.

=== ) stops at an empty line
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  "A paragraph and section boundary is also a sentence boundary."
given:
  |foo bar

  baz
keys:   )
expect:
  foo bar
  |
  baz

=== ) in the last sentence goes to the end of the buffer
ref:    motion.txt *)*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s forward."
given:  One. |Two
keys:   )
expect: One. Tw|o

=== ( goes to the start of the current sentence
ref:    motion.txt *(*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s backward.  |exclusive| motion."
given:  Hello there. How a|re you?
keys:   (
expect: Hello there. |How are you?

=== ( at the start of a sentence goes to the previous one
ref:    motion.txt *(*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s backward."
given:  One. Two. |Three.
keys:   (
expect: One. |Two. Three.

=== 2( with a count
ref:    motion.txt *(*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s backward."
given:  One. Two. Th|ree.
keys:   2(
expect: One. |Two. Three.

=== ( at the start of the buffer does not move
ref:    motion.txt *(*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s backward."
given:  |One. Two.
keys:   (
expect: |One. Two.

=== d) deletes to the next sentence, excluding it (exclusive)
ref:    motion.txt *)*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s forward.  |exclusive| motion."
given:  |One. Two.
keys:   d)
expect: |Two.
regs:   "" = "One. "

=== d( deletes back to the start of the sentence (exclusive)
ref:    motion.txt *(*
quote:  "[count] |sentence|s backward.  |exclusive| motion."
given:  One. Two |three.
keys:   d(
expect: One. |three.
regs:   "" = "Two "
